-snip">The Group Areas Act of 1950 was a central law of apartheid in South Africa that assigned separate residential and business areas in towns and cities to each racial group.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/grouville-hoard"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/grouville-hoard.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Grouville Hoard</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">The Grouville Hoard, also called the Le Câtillon II hoard, is a large Iron Age coin hoard found in 2012 at Grouville in Jersey by two metal detectorists.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/grover-cleveland"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/grover-cleveland.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Grover Cleveland</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Grover Cleveland was the 22nd and 24th president of the United States, serving from 1885 to 1889 and from 1893 to 1897.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/gruffydd-ap-gwenwynwyn"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/gruffydd-ap-gwenwynwyn.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Gruffydd ap Gwenwynwyn</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Gruffydd ap Gwenwynwyn was prince of Powys Wenwynwyn in mid-Wales in the 13th century.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/gruffydd-ap-llywelyn"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/gruffydd-ap-llywelyn.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Gruffydd ap Llywelyn</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Gruffydd ap Llywelyn was king of Gwynedd and Powys from 1039 and, from about 1055, ruler of nearly all of Wales, the only king ever to unite it.</span></a></li><li class="en