arí</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Guacanagarí was the cacique of Marién in north-western Hispaniola when Columbus arrived in 1492.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/guadalajara-mexico"><span class="enc-name">Guadalajara (Mexico)</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Guadalajara is the capital of the Mexican state of Jalisco and one of the largest cities in Mexico.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/guadalajara-spain"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/guadalajara-spain.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Guadalajara (Spain)</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Guadalajara is a city in central Spain, capital of the province of the same name in Castilla–La Mancha, on the Henares river north-east of Madrid.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/guadalcanal-campaign"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/guadalcanal-campaign.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Guadalcanal campaign</span><span class="enc-type">Campaign · 1942–1943</span><span class="enc-snip">The Guadalcanal campaign was a prolonged Allied offensive in the Solomon Islands from 1942 to 1943 during the Second World War.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/guadalentin"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/guadalentin.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Guadalentín</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">The Guadalentín is a river of south-eastern Spain, a tributary of the Segura, flowing through Lorca and the region of Murcia.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/guadalete"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/guadalete.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"